<title>USA: MBIA qualifies nine muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies nine muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp said Thursday it qualified for bond insurance the following nine municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Plainville, Conn., $2.5 million general obligations.</p>
<p>--River Grove, Ill., $1.485 million refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Woodridge, Ill., $4.95 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Grant County SDFC, Ky., $12.155 million school building bonds.</p>
<p>--Natchitoches Parish, La., $10 million school GOs.</p>
<p>--Sandwich Water District, Mass., $1.385 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Portsmouth, N.H., $3.768 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Jersey City, N.J., $30 million school bonds, direct purchase.</p>
<p>--Runnemede, N.J., $2.95 million Board of Ed bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
